.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt CROND 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm crond
.Nd minimal per-minute cron daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon reads every regular file under
.Pa /var/cron ,
parses it as a crontab, and runs matching commands once per minute through the kernel spawn
path.
.Pp
Each job logs
.Dq crond: start
and
.Dq crond: exit
with the user, command and status. A missing or empty spool is not an error.
.Pp
The scheduler is serial: a command is waited for before the next start. Overlap detection and
.Ql @reboot
are explicit unsupported cases. Shell metacharacters in a command are rejected; use a script
if redirection or pipelines are needed.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The spool directory is
.Pa /var/cron .
The image must mount a writable filesystem there; the P4y qtest mounts ramfs.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
runs until terminated. It exits non-zero only on an unrecoverable startup error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr crontab 1
.Sh STANDARDS
Five-field cron scheduling at minute granularity. `@reboot`, overlap policies and GNU
extensions are documented omissions.
